DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions return a value equivalent to

           exp(x) - 1

       The result is computed in a way that is accurate even if the value of _x
       is  near  zero—a  case where _e_x_p_(_x_) _- _1 would be inaccurate due to sub‐
       traction of two numbers that are nearly equal.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return _e_x_p_(_x_) _- _1.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.

       If _x is positive infinity, positive infinity is returned.

       If _x is negative infinity, -1 is returned.

       If the result overflows, a range error occurs, and the functions return
       -HHUUGGEE__VVAALL, -HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or -HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively.

