BBUUGGSS
       Before glibc 2.17, on certain architectures (e.g., x86, but not x86_64)
       eexxppmm11() raised a bogus underflow floating‐point exception for some
       large negative _x values (where the function result approaches -1).

       Before approximately glibc 2.11, eexxppmm11() raised a bogus invalid
       floating‐point exception in addition to the expected overflow
       exception, and returned a NaN instead of positive infinity, for some
       large positive _x values.

       Before glibc 2.11, the glibc implementation did not set _e_r_r_n_o to EERRAANNGGEE
       when a range error occurred.

